[b]WitcherFG 0.1.0-preview.1 — unpublished preview[/b]

WitcherFG attempts guarded, temporary Streamline import routing for The Witcher 3 Xbox PC package 5.0.4.0. No stable release or public download/support URL is available. Player packaging and exact-candidate gameplay/install/upgrade/uninstall acceptance are Pending.

The earlier RTX 5070 Ti / driver 617.42 / Windows 26200 / 1440p diagnostic probe restored FG/MFG with manual ray tracing recovery. That probe does not verify the native launcher or a player ZIP. Applied and RoutingAlreadyPresent confirm routing only; FPS ratios do not prove generated frames.

For a developer-built executable, close the game, keep the utility outside the game directory on a fixed local drive, and run WitcherFG.exe. Preserve existing game/mod DLLs and backups. No chainloading or manager coexistence is verified. Unknown builds and late startup refuse.

Error logging is the default; automatic runtime observation is Off. The SDK diagnostic catalog is empty, so unavailable activity fields remain Unknown. Explicit WitcherFG.exe --collect-support creates a local sanitized archive without uploads. Forced watchdog 1460/fallback 124 and immediate unsafe helper 3 bypass normal returned exits 0/2/3/4; helper death does not prove target exit or detach.

This unpublished draft uses docs/release-summary.md as its canonical player-facing source. Detailed compatibility, installation, uninstall, diagnostics and troubleshooting sources accompany the repository. Automated rendering/packaging is pending; no Nexus page, public issue form or download link is claimed.
